ing October 1, 2025, SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing services accessed via the outdated URLs will experience reduced performance. To avoid this, ensure you switch to the new URLs before that date.  For more information, see Calculation, Data Upload, Administration, Data Access, Coupon Management.  It is also recommended to recreate the service keys. This way, you can see the new URL of the service endpoint in the service key. For more information about creating service keys, see Creating Service Keys in the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 374 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Meta attribute mapping reordered\nDescription: The meta attribute mapping is reordered to come before the meta.location attribute mapping in the proxy read transformations of Cloud Foundry UAA Server and SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry). This ensures that the meta.location attribute is set correctly and is not overwritten.  Additionally, the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:Group extension schema is added for the group entity in the proxy read transformations of SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry).  For more information, see:    Cloud Foundry UAA Server  SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: 28120\n\n--- Record 375 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: 28120\n\n--- Record 376 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management supports userUUID\nDescription: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management now supports provisioning of users with the userUUID attribute. The default read, write and proxy read and write transformations are enhanced to handle the universally unique identifier.  For more information, see SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: 28120\n\n--- Record 377 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Meta attribute mapping reordered\nDescription: The meta attribute mapping is reordered to come before the meta.location attribute mapping in the proxy read transformations of Cloud Foundry UAA Server and SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry). This ensures that the meta.location attribute is set correctly and is not overwritten.  Additionally, the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:Group extension schema is added for the group entity in the proxy read transformations of SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry).  For more information, see:    Cloud Foundry UAA Server  SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 378 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management supports userUUID\nDescription: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management now supports provisioning of users with the userUUID attribute. The default read, write and proxy read and write transformations are enhanced to handle the universally unique identifier.  For more information, see SAP Ariba Central Invoice", "2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 378 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management supports userUUID\nDescription: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management now supports provisioning of users with the userUUID attribute. The default read, write and proxy read and write transformations are enhanced to handle the universally unique identifier.  For more information, see SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-29\nValid as Of: 2025-07-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 379 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Custom OIDC configuration as a list of oidc objects\nDescription: When provisioning or updating your Kyma runtime, you can now configure the OpenID Connect (OIDC) property as a list of oidc objects. With this setting, you can have multiple OIDC configurations in your cluster. You can also see your complete OIDC configuration in the SAP BTP cockpit.  To ensure you have the necessary attributes for smooth authentication and to prevent access issues, we have added the requiredClaims and groupsPrefix fields to the oidc object.  For more information, see Custom OpenID Connect Configuration and OpenID Connect (OIDC).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 380 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: New provisioning parameter: Colocate Control Plane\nDescription: With the Colocate Control Plane parameter (technical name: colocateControlPlane), you can enforce the location of the control plane in the same region where your cluster's worker nodes are deployed, and thus control where your sensitive data is stored and processed.  For more information, see Provisioning and Updating Parameters in the Kyma Environment and Available Plans in the Kyma Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1531 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Keda module: Update to version 1.6.0\nDescription: In this release, we have updated KEDA to version 2.16.1.  In addition, we have added the status widget with conditions to the details view in Kyma dashboard for Keda CR and ScaledObject CR.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-16\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1532 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Task Center Improvements\nDescription:   Improved the back navigation when returning from the Substitution Management screen in the SAP Task Center Web app.  Internal optimizations and refactoring to ensure performance, security, and future improvements.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-29\nValid as Of: 2025-01-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1533 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of MTA Build Tool Version Java 8 Node 18\nDescription: The MTA build tool version Java 8 Node 18 is deprecated and has been removed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1534 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of the Container-Based Applications Pipeline\nDescription:  The Container-Based Applications pipeline has been deprecated and is no longer available for use. While your existing jobs can still be viewed, you will not be able to run or edit them anymore.  We recommend using the Kyma Runtime pipeline instead.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1535 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Increased Quotas\nDescription: For the default and build-code service plans, the limit of job configurations and the maximum number of connected repositories have been increased from 500 to 1000.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1536 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for New File Types (Premium Edition)\nDescription: SAP Document AI now supports businessCard, invoice, paymentAdvice, purchaseOrder, and custom documents in the following file types:  DOC  DOCM  DOCX  DOT  DOTM  DOTX  EML  EMLX  MSG  ODT  OFT  OLM  PAGES  RTF  TXT    See Supported File Types (Embedded Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1537 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for the Identity Authentication Service\nDescription: You can now subscribe to the SAP Document AI basic UI using the Identity Authentication service to handle authentication and authorization tasks in SAP BTP.  See Subscribing to the SAP Document AI Basic UI With the Identity Authentication Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-28\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1538 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.25.0. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1539 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: All SAP SuccessFactors Use Cases Upgraded to New Conversational Experience in Joule\nDescription: Based on the new conversational experience, SAP SuccessFactors has introduced a new transactional use case and upgraded all remaining cases. For more information, refer to All Use Cases Upgraded to New Conversational Experience in Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Human Resources\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-17\nValid as Of: 2025-01-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1540 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use two new functions, SUBSTRING and STRINGREPLACE in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-27\nValid as Of: 2025-01-27", "01-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1540 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use two new functions, SUBSTRING and STRINGREPLACE in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-27\nValid as Of: 2025-01-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 101 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Offboard data\nDescription: You can now use the Migration API to offboard data from the SAP Document Management service without causing data loss.  See Offboarding Data from SAP Document Management Service in the Multi-Cloud Foundation  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-09-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 102 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.19\nDescription: New and changed features are available for .  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.19. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-16\nValid as Of: 2025-09-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 103 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: SAP Document Management Service is supported as a repository type for the orchestration grounding module.  For more information, see Create a Generic Secret for AI Data Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-15\nValid as Of: 2025-09-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 104 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Access to Runtime Parameters\nDescription: Runtime Parameters has been removed from Quick Links. You can now access Runtime Parameters only through Component Monitor.See: Runtime Parameters\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 105 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configure Istio Proxy Resources\nDescription: Manually increase resource limits for Istio Proxies for the worker component.See: Set Ixtio Proxy Resources\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 106 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Edge Local Authentication and Authorization Support for External Certificate Pinning.\nDescription: When pinning is disabled for external client certificates, the system doesn't accept a previously used certificate with an older issue date for authentication once you use a renewed certificate.  See: Edge Local Authentication and Authorization\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 107 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enabling ADK persistency with apadter API Available\nDescription: You can now utilize an adapter API to store and retrieve critical information ensuring data persistence even after node restarts or crashes.  See Enabling ADK Persistency\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 108 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Action in Job Management\nDescription: A new action, Consolidate MPL Aggregation Data, is available in Job Management.See: Job Management\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 109 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Reusable API Artifact\nDescription: You can now create reusable API artifacts that encapsulate standardized API policies and mediation logic such as authentication, transformation, and validation into modular units. These artifacts can be defined centrally and used across multiple API artifacts, helping you maintain consistency and streamline API development.   See, Reusable API Artifact  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 110 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: RFC Adapter Receiver Supported in Diagnostics\nDescription: The Adapter diagnostics task now also supports the RFC adapter with receiver direction.See: Diagnostics\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-14\nValid as Of: 2025-09-14\nVersion: 2507\n\n", "--- Record 311 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Text Generation & Summarization Using AI\nDescription: A new set of AI features is now available for you to use in your workpages:      AI summarization      AI comment generation      AI text generationNote  This feature is only available in a preview environment.      These features will be available for a limited period until 31st December 2025 and will be offered as a promotional model that will allow you to use it without charge. The same promotional model applies to enhancements to these features during the promotional period.  You will be entitled to trigger up to 100,000 requests per calendar month across all SAP Build Work Zone instances within your SAP BTP global account.  Once the promotional period ends, you can continue using the AI features under the commercial model that’s in place. If you don't enable the commercial model after the promotional period ends, the feature is automatically disabled.  For more information, see Enabling AI Features  and How to Use AI features to Create Content.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: 2507B\n\n--- Record 312 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Configurations API – Ability to Set Default Values\nDescription: There is a new input field author for endpoints PATCH /configurations/{configurationId}/items/{itemId}/characteristics/{characteristicId} and PATCH /configurations/{configurationId}/items/{itemId} that allows not only to set user values for characteristics as before, but also so-called default values that can be changed by users and can be overwritten by rules.   Note  It is not supported for AVC Forwarding and only in exceptional cases it makes sense to set defaults via API.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 313 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Configurations API – Map New AVC Author\nDescription: AVC introduced the new author 7 for characteristic values that have been set through classification. During AVC forwarding, this unknown author used to cause an error when processing AVC’s configuration results. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 314 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Configurations API – Persist User Values Involved in Conflicts\nDescription: Setting a user value for a characteristic that has already a system value assigned causes a conflict. Such a conflict used not to be returned in all cases. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 315 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automatic Version Selection in Job Creation\nDescription: When creating a new job, the latest pipeline version is now automatically selected. To simplify the job creation process, the version selection drop-down has been removed.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 316 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: APIRule v1beta1 deletion timeline\nDescription: APIRule custom resource (CR) v1beta1 has been deprecated and scheduled for deletion. The following timeline outlines the steps we will take to phase out version v1beta1:  Kyma dashboard won't display APIRule CRs in version v1beta1. All APIRules v1beta1 will be fully operational from the command line, and you will still be able to manage them using kubectl. This change will not affect any pipelines that manage APIRules using Kubernetes utilities such as kubectl or helm.    Fast channel release date: August 18, 2025  Regular channel release date: September 1, 2025      You won't be able to create APIRule CRs v1beta1 in new clusters. In existing clusters, you will still be able to create and modify APIRule CRs v1beta1.  Fast channel release date: End of October, 2025  Regular channel release date: Mid-November, 2025    You won't be able to create APIRule CRs v1beta1 in new and existing clusters, modify existing APIRule CRs v1beta1, or delete them. All APIRule v1beta1 configurations set up prior to this restriction will remain active and continue to function as expected. The API Gateway module will manage and reconcile resources based on the existing APIRule settings.  Fast channel release date: Mid-November, 2025  Regular channel release date: End of the year 2025      Required action: Migrate all your APIRules to version v2. To learn how to do this, see APIRule Migration. We strongly recommend that you start the migration as soon as possible to avoid any disruptions.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability", " to function as expected. The API Gateway module will manage and reconcile resources based on the existing APIRule settings.  Fast channel release date: Mid-November, 2025  Regular channel release date: End of the year 2025      Required action: Migrate all your APIRules to version v2. To learn how to do this, see APIRule Migration. We strongly recommend that you start the migration as soon as possible to avoid any disruptions.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 317 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Local Extension – Extension Display Correction\nDescription: In the Administrative UI, extensions with numbers longer than three digits were incorrectly shown as not executable in the Active Local Extensions section. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-27\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 318 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Identity Directory SCIM API\nDescription: You can create users with password hash attributes via the Identity Directory SCIM API. You can also specify your own hashing algorithm details during user creation. The following attributes are now available for use in the Identity Directory SCIM API: passwordHash, passwordHashAlgorithm, passwordHashSalt, passwordHashCycles, totpSecret, totpFailedAttempts, totpLockedTime . See Overview | Identity Directory API | SAP Business Accelerator Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: 28165\n\n--- Record 319 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Mandatory email for job subscribers\nDescription: A message in the UI now ensures that all subscribers for job notifications provide an email address.\nAction: I